  "worked_solution": "We are given the last term of our series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}({a}_{1}+{a}_{N}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, ${a}_{N}$ is the last term, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting ${a}_{18}=-62$, $N=18$, and ${S}_{N}=-495$ into the formula above and solving for ${a}_{1}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-495 & =\\frac{18}{2}({a}_{1}-62) \\\\ -495 & =9({a}_{1}-62) \\\\ \\frac{-495}{9} & ={a}_{1}-62 \\\\ -55 & ={a}_{1}-62 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
